# pip-audit ignore list
# Format: one vulnerability ID per line (CVE-*, PYSEC-*, GHSA-*)
# Each entry has a justification comment on the preceding line(s).
#
# Original triage: 2026-05-20 (Code, security hardening LB-10)
# Last re-verified: 2026-07-31 (Code, launch VAPT Gate 1, MHQ-801)
#
# Rating key:
#   ACCEPT  -- not exploitable in Morse's context
#   MONITOR -- unclear exploitability, track for future review
#
# Re-verification rule: an entry earns its place only while pip-audit still
# reports it. A stale entry is worse than no entry — it silently re-suppresses
# the finding if the dependency ever regresses to a vulnerable version. Run
# bare `uv run pip-audit` (no --ignore-vuln) and drop anything it no longer
# reports.
#
# That rule is now ENFORCED by scripts/check-audit-ignore.py, which runs in CI
# and weekly. It fails on two things this file previously relied on someone
# remembering:
#   * an ID a bare audit no longer reports (STALE — delete the line)
#   * an entry past its `# expires:` date (re-verify, or drop it)
#
# Every ID needs an `# expires: YYYY-MM-DD` on a preceding comment line. One
# date governs the run of IDs beneath it, so a triage batch shares a review-by
# date. Ninety days is the working default: long enough not to be busywork,
# short enough that "not exploitable in our context" is re-judged against a
# codebase that has actually changed since.
#
# 2026-07-31 re-verification: bare pip-audit reports 4 findings in exactly 1
# package (pip). Every non-pip entry from the 2026-05-20 triage was dropped —
# the vulnerable versions are gone from the resolved tree:
#   pygments 2.20.0, idna 3.18, lxml 6.1.1, pillow 12.3.0, langsmith 0.9.4,
#   click 8.4.2, urllib3 2.7.0 (the requests>=2.33 bump pulled the fix, as the
#   original urllib3 comment predicted), requests 2.34.2.
# The two "version bump attempted but reverted" entries (click, pillow) are
# resolved too — those bumps have since landed on their own.

# 2026-09-06 re-verification: the three pip entries below (CVE-2026-3219,
# CVE-2026-6357, PYSEC-2026-196) are STALE — a bare `pip-audit` no longer
# reports them, meaning the base image's pip has moved past the vulnerable
# 26.0.1 build referenced in the 2026-07-31 note. Deleted per this file's
# own enforced rule (scripts/check-audit-ignore.py) rather than left to
# silently re-suppress a future regression.

